# 2.1) Create the Dataset and Tabs

On this page, you will create the dashboard, the `{{ ds_main.name }}` dataset, and two tabs for widgets to use.

## Task 1 - Create a dashboard

1. Click **New** in the left sidebar, then click **Dashboard**.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-01-new-dashboard.png', 'New > Dashboard') }}

2. Click the dashboard name at the top (**New Dashboard ...**) and enter `<your_name> - {{ s.naming.dashboard }}`. For example, if your name is {{ s.naming.example_user | capitalize }}, enter `{{ s.naming.example_user }} - {{ s.naming.dashboard }}`.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-02-dashboard-name.png', 'Enter dashboard name') }}

## Task 2 - Create a dataset { #task-2 }

Dashboard widgets are based on **datasets**. {{ ds_main.intro }}

1. Click the **Data** tab at the top.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-03-data-tab.png', 'Data tab') }}

2. Click **Add SQL dataset**.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-04-create-from-sql.png', 'Create from SQL') }}

3. Paste the query below into the SQL editor. Replace `{{ ex_cat }}` with your own catalog name.

    ```sql title="{{ ds_main.name }} dataset"
    --8<-- "lab-files/eng/step2/{{ ds_main.file }}"
    ```

4. Click **Run** to execute the query and check that the results table appears below.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-05-dataset-run.png', 'Dataset query execution result') }}

5. Click the dataset name (**Untitled dataset**) in the left dataset list and rename it to `{{ ds_main.name }}`.

    {{ shot('02-aibi-dashboard/2-1-06-dataset-rename.png', 'Rename dataset') }}

